# J1: build the TP4-capable serving image (no card is opened)
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the TP4 bring-up (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env, commit, and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock; the workflow's step limits in parentheses): drift 5-15 min (step 20), build 30-70 min (step 75), probe 15-40 min (step 50): about 60-125 min at most; the build alone is one step of at most 75 min.
# Holds the exclusive group while it runs although it opens no card: queue it when the cards are idle anyway. Check df first: a new image is ~32 GB, and the (1, 4) weight cache is a new ~28 GiB on first boot.
C2_ACTIONS=drift build probe
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-g1-1
C2_PROFILE=general-tp4
